      "problem": "Compute $\\textrm E[5X-2Y]$ if $\\textrm E[X]=1$ and $\\textrm E[Y] = 2.$",
      "worked_solution": "For any random variables $X,Y$ and any constants $a,b,$ we have\n\n$$\n\\textrm E[aX+bY] = a \\textrm E[X] + b \\textrm E[Y].\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{E}[5X-2Y] & =5\\text{E}[X]-2\\text{E}[Y] \\\\  & =5(1)-2(2) \\\\  & =1.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
